      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be clearer to just make the range member actually be the number of bits to shift right?\n\nrange\u0027s interpretation seems sensor specific... (or is there some representation that\u0027s required by higher levels, e.g. sysfs,iio?)\n\nIt just seems weird to me to call set_range with (1 \u003c\u003c 18) as the range when that\u0027s not the range. And if it\u0027s not the actual range, why not just make it the number to shift right?\n\n\nOr... maybe I\u0027m completely wrong and that is indeed the range. :)",
      "revId": "1dedbed05a39b4c3698506b7c2deb9ad30605913",
